name 'building-data-driven-systems-postassessment-q1_2025'

question 'A developer is building a "Favorites" feature where users can add and remove items. Which statement best explains why an array is necessary for this feature?'

wrong 'Arrays are the only way to save data permanently to a hard drive.'
right 'Arrays allow the app to treat a group of items as a single collection that can grow or shrink as the user interacts with it.'
wrong 'Arrays automatically sort data alphabetically, which users expect in a favorites list.'
wrong 'Variables cannot store strings, so an array is needed to hold the names of favorite items.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 1

Arrays provide the structure needed to manage dynamic collections. Unlike individual variables, arrays can expand (using `.push()`) or contract (using `.pop()`) based on user actions. 
MARKDOWN
